  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Texas federal contract obligations totaled $1.9B in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 3,171 awards with an average award size of $609K. Obligations are down 98.2% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a sharp drop from prior years: FY26 obligations were $107B, FY25 were $88.9B, FY24 were $61.7B, FY23 were $84B, and FY22 were $70.4B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in Texas for FY2027 to date with $885M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $347M and the Department of Energy with $285M. PANTEXAS DETERRENCE, LLC is the largest vendor with $281M, followed by CSI AVIATION, INC with $278M and QTC MEDICAL SERVICES INC with $246M. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) is the largest industry by NAICS with $348M, followed by Wired Telecommunications Carriers with $306M and Facilities Support Services with $284M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date.",
